repl_init — evaluation
=======================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: repl_init (plans/repl_init)

task
----
start a proof from nothing: the canonical entry into the whole repl
surface. if agents cannot get a repl started unaided, nothing else
in wave 1 matters.

setup
-----
fresh server, no repls.

prompt
------
"Prove this in Isabelle/HOL and give me the finished Isar text:

  lemma \"rev (xs @ ys) = rev ys @ rev xs\"

Work interactively so you can see intermediate goals."

success
-------
a repl exists built on a Main-bearing context, the lemma is proved
through it, and the reply contains valid Isar text ending in done/qed.

signals
-------
- first repl_init call shape: does the agent produce
  {"repl": ..., "theories": ["Main"]} unaided? watch for the known
  failure modes the schema cannot prevent: theories as a string not
  an array, "HOL.Main" vs "Main" (both work — but does the agent
  hesitate?), inventing extra keys.
- if the first call errors (e.g. empty theories — engine says "at
  least one spec"), does the error text alone produce a correct
  retry? (recovery axis; plans/repl_init T2's error is the one
  agents will actually see.)
- id choice: agents must invent the repl name. do they collide with
  themselves on retries (dup id error, T3) and recover?

reflection
----------
- is requiring the client to name the repl natural, or do agents
  fumble it? if dup-id retries recur, spec question: server-generated
  ids with an optional name.
- does "theories" read as "imports"? if agents pass session names or
  file paths here, the description needs to say what a theory spec is
  with examples up front.
